ont-page news in the  Netherlands because I've been  corresponding by email with the author  of a biography of Anne Frank and she  wrote a book about otto Frank and we  correspondent about this and I have some  young married friends who live in  Netherlands and they told me it was  front-page news you know like our  sensational news items it was on TV all  the time day and night so maybe they'll  someday find out who the betrayer was  that's a good question Joe thank you  look I have two questions and one of  them is the Anne Frank House was that  the one turned into a museum or did they  build like a little house and then put  the items in it no that's a good  question the actual place where the  family hid for two years is now a museum  and mr. Frank said he didn't want  anything changed know those pictures on  the wall those postcards from Anne's  collection they're still there I think  they have a glass covering to protect  them but it's exactly the way it was the  day they left and he wanted to kept just  that way now in addition they've added a  Study Center and a bookshop you know  places where students can go and look at  books look at books about Anne Frank  about other historical matters but the  actual hiding place is kept just the way  it was and you walk up the little narrow  staircase just the way the Franks did  it's an amazing experience I hope you  get to go there someday do you have  another question my second question was  that it's it that there was a bookshelf  and it swung open it was the doorway how  did the Nazis find that that's exactly  what Joe is saying they are sure that  somebody betrayed the Franks somebody  knew that that secret bookcase you know  was like a secret door that opened  because when the police came in they  didn't kind of roam around they went  right for that bookcase that was that  concealed the annex where they were  hiding and to this day they've never  found out who it was who knew who tipped  off the Nazi police do you know that  rewards were given money rewards were  given for any Jews that were captured so  maybe somebody turned in the Franks for  a money reward it's a kind of horrible  thing but that might have happened but  nobody knows for sure some other  questions well again I want to thank you  so so much for being a wonderful  audience and so responsive and I look  forward to seeing you  and I hope that you read this book and  other books and if you haven't read the  diary and if you haven't read the play  and the revision of the play I hope  you'll go back and read it because there  are no words like the words of Anne  Frank thank you again Susan Goldman  rubens books searching for Anne Frank  letters from Amsterdam to Iowa is  published by Abrams books for young  readers visit them on the web at abrams  books com
 

